@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il30-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-88-definitions`
IMPORT `ito-125b-dividends`

-- Tests for s 125B (the rate of tax on a dividend). Every rate was read from the section (25% or 30%, source lines 4514-4518) and the
-- tax worked as rate x dividend by hand before it was run. A failing assertion is a finding. All holdings are HYPOTHETICAL.

§ `Tests of section 125B`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons`
`a profits holding of` f MEANS
    `Holdings of means of control in one body of persons` WITH
        `fraction of the right to profits`                                              IS f
        `fraction of the right to appoint a director or general manager`                IS 0
        `fraction of the voting rights in the general meeting`                          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to a share of the surplus assets on winding up`          IS 0
        `fraction of the right to direct the holder of a right in (1) to (4) on how to use it` IS 0

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A person who may hold together with the person`
`a sibling's profits holding of` f MEANS
    `A person who may hold together with the person` WITH
        `holdings` IS `a profits holding of` f
        `tie to the person` IS `a tie of paragraph (1)` `sibling`
        `regularly cooperates with the person by agreement on material matters of the body` IS FALSE

GIVETH A LIST OF `A person who may hold together with the person`
`no others` MEANS EMPTY

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The holdings of a person on one day`
`a profits record on` d `of` f MEANS
    `The holdings of a person on one day` WITH
        `the day` IS d
        `the person's own holdings that day` IS `a profits holding of` f
        `the others who may hold together with the person that day` IS `no others`

-- Own holding f, two siblings with g each.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A NUMBER
      g IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The holdings of a person on one day`
`a profits record on` d `of` f `with two siblings of` g MEANS
    `The holdings of a person on one day` WITH
        `the day` IS d
        `the person's own holdings that day` IS `a profits holding of` f
        `the others who may hold together with the person that day` IS LIST `a sibling's profits holding of` g, `a sibling's profits holding of` g

GIVEN s1 IS A `A reading of "together with another"`
      s4 IS A `A reading of the twelve months before a day`
      d1 IS A `A reading of the time at which section 125B(3) tests the shareholding`
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
`the readings:` s1 `, the twelve months` s4 `, the time of the test` d1 MEANS
    `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C` WITH
        `together with another`                   IS s1
        `counting the days of a period`           IS `declined where the way of counting changes the answer`
        `half the holding expenses`               IS `declined where half the holding expenses changes the answer`
        `the twelve months before a day`          IS s4
        `the years from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)` IS `declined where the number of years changes the answer`
        `the years from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)` IS `declined where the number of years changes the answer`
        `a cap where the gain stands in several bands` IS `declined where the way of applying the cap changes the answer`
        `where each part stands in the top layer` IS `declined where the order of the parts changes the answer`
        `the time of the test in section 125B(3)` IS d1
        `the time of the test in section 91(b)(3)` IS `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer`
        `the real gain for the middle part` IS `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer`
        `the naming of a tax year of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS `declined where the naming of the tax year changes the answer`

`the default readings` MEANS
    `the readings:` `declined where the number of others changes the answer` `, the twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer` `, the time of the test` `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`

`the readings with the first twelve-month day` MEANS
    `the readings:` `declined where the number of others changes the answer` `, the twelve months` `the twelve months begin on the day twelve months before` `, the time of the test` `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`

`the readings with the second twelve-month day` MEANS
    `the readings:` `declined where the number of others changes the answer` `, the twelve months` `the twelve months begin on the day after the day twelve months before` `, the time of the test` `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`

`the readings with any number of others` MEANS
    `the readings:` `together with any number of others, their holdings added` `, the twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer` `, the time of the test` `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`

`the readings with one other only` MEANS
    `the readings:` `together with one other person only` `, the twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer` `, the time of the test` `declined where the time of the test changes the answer`

`the readings with the test at receipt only` MEANS
    `the readings:` `declined where the number of others changes the answer` `, the twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer` `, the time of the test` `at the time of receiving the dividend only`

`the readings with the test over twelve months` MEANS
    `the readings:` `declined where the number of others changes the answer` `, the twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer` `, the time of the test` `at the time of receiving the dividend or at some time in the twelve months before it`

`the readings with the test at any time` MEANS
    `the readings:` `declined where the number of others changes the answer` `, the twelve months` `declined where the first day of the twelve months changes the answer` `, the time of the test` `at any time up to the receiving of the dividend`

`the day of the dividend` MEANS YMD 2026 6 30

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
GIVETH A `The recipient of a dividend, for section 125B`
`an individual with the records` rs MEANS `an individual` rs

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
GIVETH A `The recipient of a dividend, for section 125B`
`a family company whose 64A person has the records` rs MEANS `a family company` rs

GIVEN rs IS A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
GIVETH A `The recipient of a dividend, for section 125B`
`a non-resident body with the records` rs MEANS `a non-resident body of persons` rs

GIVETH A LIST OF `The holdings of a person on one day`
`no records` MEANS EMPTY

§§ `Paragraphs (1) and (2): an individual`
-- No record: 25%. A record of 10% on the day of the dividend: 30%. A record of 9.99%: 25%.
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 25%
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the day of the dividend` `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 30%
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the day of the dividend` `of` (9.99%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 25%
-- Twelve months before 30 June 2026: from 30 June 2025 (first reading) or 1 July 2025 (second).
--   a record on 29 June 2025: outside both: 25%.  a record on 30 June 2025: inside the first only: refused by default, 30% / 25% by name.
--   a record on 1 July 2025: inside both: 30%.
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 6 29) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 25%
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 7 1) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 30%
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "whether the recipient was a material shareholder depends on a reading section 88 leaves open, and here the rate turns on it"
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the readings with the first twelve-month day` EQUALS 30%
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 6 30) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the readings with the second twelve-month day` EQUALS 25%
-- A record after the dividend is not looked at: 25%.
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2026 7 1) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 25%
-- S1: 4% and two siblings of 4% (12% with both, 8% with one) on the day: refused by default; 30% with any number, 25% with one only.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the day of the dividend` `of` (4%) `with two siblings of` (4%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "whether the recipient was a material shareholder depends on a reading section 88 leaves open, and here the rate turns on it"
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the day of the dividend` `of` (4%) `with two siblings of` (4%))) `, reading the forks as` `the readings with any number of others` EQUALS 30%
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the day of the dividend` `of` (4%) `with two siblings of` (4%))) `, reading the forks as` `the readings with one other only` EQUALS 25%
-- 6% and two siblings of 4% (10% with one): both readings say material: 30% by default.
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the day of the dividend` `of` (6%) `with two siblings of` (4%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 30%

§§ `Paragraph (3): a family company (fork D1)`
-- The 64A person's record is on the day of the dividend: tested at receipt or over twelve months, material: 30% on every reading.
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a family company whose 64A person has the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the day of the dividend` `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 30%
-- No record: 25%.
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a family company whose 64A person has the records` `no records`) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 25%
-- A record only on 1 January 2026, six months before: at receipt only 25%; over the twelve months 30%; the default refuses.
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a family company whose 64A person has the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the readings with the test at receipt only` EQUALS 25%
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a family company whose 64A person has the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the readings with the test over twelve months` EQUALS 30%
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a family company whose 64A person has the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 125B(3) names no time at which the shareholding is tested, and here the rate turns on it"
-- 1 January 2025 is eighteen months before the dividend, outside the twelve months on two readings but inside the third (0.1.1, fork D1: "was", with no limit of time):
-- at receipt only 25%, over the twelve months 25%, at any time 30%: the readings part, so the default declines.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a family company whose 64A person has the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 1 1) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 125B(3) names no time at which the shareholding is tested, and here the rate turns on it"
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a family company whose 64A person has the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 1 1) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the readings with the test at receipt only` EQUALS 25%
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a family company whose 64A person has the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 1 1) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the readings with the test over twelve months` EQUALS 25%
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a family company whose 64A person has the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 1 1) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the readings with the test at any time` EQUALS 30%
-- A holding on the day of the dividend is inside every reading: 30% by default.

§§ `Paragraph (4): a public institution or a provident fund`
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a public institution or a provident fund as defined in section 9(2)` FALSE) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 25%
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a public institution or a provident fund as defined in section 9(2)` TRUE) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 125B(4) sets a rate only for a dividend that is not exempt in the hands of the recipient"

§§ `Paragraph (5): a non-resident body of persons`
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a non-resident body with the records` `no records`) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 25%
-- A record 11 months before (30 July 2025): inside the twelve months on every reading: 30%.
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`a non-resident body with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` (YMD 2025 7 30) `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 30%

§§ `Any other recipient, and the date`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` `any other recipient` `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "section 125B has no paragraph for this recipient"
-- A dividend received on 31 December 2011 is before the change date: declined. On 1 January 2012: answered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` (YMD 2011 12 31) `by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` BECAUSE "the deposited text of section 125B is the text as amended in 2012, and the text before it is not deposited"
#ASSERT `s 125B — the rate of tax on a dividend received on` (YMD 2012 1 1) `by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 25%

§§ `The tax`
-- 40,000 x 25% = 10,000 ; 40,000 x 30% = 12,000.
#ASSERT `s 125B — the tax on a dividend of` 40_000 `received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` `no records`) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT `s 125B — the tax on a dividend of` 40_000 `received on` `the day of the dividend` `by` (`an individual with the records` (LIST `a profits record on` `the day of the dividend` `of` (10%))) `, reading the forks as` `the default readings` EQUALS 12_000
